{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% block content %}
<div class="card" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Working draft — to be finalized before public launch (see LAUNCH.md).</p>

  <h3>What we collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account data:</strong> your email address and a hashed password. Optionally an agency name, accent color, and logo you upload for report branding.</li>
    <li><strong>Scan data:</strong> URLs of pages on sites you add, detected accessibility issues, and short HTML snippets of the flagged elements — all from publicly reachable pages.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing data:</strong> handled by Stripe. We store only Stripe's customer and subscription identifiers, never card numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>Operational logs:</strong> standard server logs (IP, path, timestamp) kept briefly for security and debugging.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What we don't do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No advertising, no selling or sharing data with data brokers.</li>
    <li>No tracking scripts or analytics beacons injected into scanned sites — scanning is read-only.</li>
    <li>No storage of your clients' visitor data; we never see it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Deletion</h3>
  <p>Deleting a site removes its scans, issues, and share links immediately. Deleting your
  account removes everything, including your logo file. Backups age out within 30 days.</p>

  <h3>Subprocessors</h3>
  <p>Hosting provider (server location listed at launch), Stripe (payments), and our
  transactional email provider (password resets and scan alerts). Each processes only what it
  needs to.</p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>Questions or data requests: <a href="mailto:{{ supportEmail }}">{{ supportEmail }}</a></p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
